# Git workflow (Job Talentio)

Also follow `.cursor/rules/development-lifecycle.mdc` (CI/CD + staging/prod gates).

## Long-lived branches

| Branch | Role | Railway env |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `develop` | Integration / staging | `staging` (auto-deploy) |
| `main` | Production-ready | `production` (auto-deploy) |

- Never commit directly to `main` or `develop`.
- Never force-push `main` or `develop`.
- Remote: `https://github.com/EGI-HOLDING/job-talentio.git`

## Day-to-day work

1. Start from up-to-date `develop`, then create a short-lived branch:
   - `feature/<short-kebab-name>` | `fix/...` | `chore/...`
   - Hotfix from `main`: `hotfix/<name>`
2. Implement the requested work on that branch.
3. **Ship automatically** (see below) — do not stop and ask.
4. Wait for CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`); fix failures on the same branch.
5. Prefer squash merge; delete the branch after merge.
6. After merge, staging redeploys from `develop` — verify there before any prod release.

## Agent: auto commit + push + PR (mandatory)

This repo opts out of “wait for the user to ask before committing.”

After finishing a coherent unit of work (feature, fix, or chore), **always** do this without asking:

1. **Commit** relevant files (never secrets: `.env`, credentials, private keys).
   - Message: concise, why > what; match recent `git log` style.
   - PowerShell: `git commit -m @"...multiline..."@` (no interactive `-i`).
   - **No AI attribution:** never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or `git commit --trailer` (see `no-ai-commit-attribution.mdc`).
2. **Push** the branch: `git push -u origin HEAD` (needs network/`all` permissions).
3. **Open a PR into `develop`** with `gh pr create` if one does not already exist for this branch.
   - Title + body with Summary + Test plan.
   - Target is always **`develop`**, never `main`.
   - No Cursor/AI attribution in the PR title, body, or comments; verify with `gh pr view` after creating (see `no-ai-commit-attribution.mdc`).
   - When squash-merging, pass explicit `--subject`/`--body` so old commit trailers cannot leak into the squash message.

Do **not**:

- Wait for “lanjutkan / commit dulu / buat PR” unless the user said **hold**, **jangan commit**, or **jangan push**.
- Push or merge to `main` unless the user explicitly requests a production release.
- Skip hooks (`--no-verify`) or force-push protected branches.
- Commit unrelated dirty files (e.g. line-ending-only `infra/*.example`).
- Include Cursor/AI co-author or Made-with trailers in commits or PRs.

If a PR for the branch already exists, push new commits and leave the existing PR (update the body only when scope changed materially).

## Release / hotfix

- **Release:** user asks → PR `develop` → `main` → optional tag `vX.Y.Z`.
- **Hotfix:** branch from `main` → PR to `main` → sync back to `develop`.
